==Scottish Gaelic==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gd|sga|alt||shore, cliff}}. Cognates in the Celtic languages include {{cog|ga|alt||height, glenside, cliff}}, {{cog|kw|als||cliff}}, and {{cog|br|aot||shore}}. MacBain suggests the Scottish Gaelic form and meaning has a Pictish origin.

===Pronunciation===
{{IPA|gd|/auɫ̪t/}}

===Noun===
{{gd-noun|g=m|gen=uillt|pl=uillt}}

# [[stream]]
#: {{ux|gd|Tha an t-'''allt''' a' ruith.|inline=1|The stream is flowing.}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|gd|alltan||burn, brook, stream}}

===References===
* {{R:Dwelly}}
* {{R:MacBain}}

{{topics|gd|Geography|Water}}

